      "writtenOn": "2023-10-24T12:15:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I wonder if this is the right place for this? Our teardown logic is very complex, especially with unregisterAfterReplacement and delayed teardown.\n\nIn particular, when unregisterAfterReplacement is used, destroyNetwork is called much before this code runs. It seems like maybe we should call maybeDisableForwardRulesForDisconnectingNai in destroyNetwork instead of here?\n\nNot sure though what would happen if then that network is selected by some other local network\u0027s upstream. Maybe the forwarding rule code should check whether the upstream isDestroyed() and if so do nothing?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 4941,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 4941,
        "endChar": 51
      },
      "revId": "f88210634d5658f9f0108e7193d100dd6e8b774e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
